cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TrafficTwin Jeddah, please cite it as below. Results are synthetic demand, uncalibrated."
title: "TrafficTwin Jeddah: an open-source city traffic digital twin, policy lab and emergency decision support"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Tariq
    family-names: Alturkestani
  - name: "The TrafficTwin Jeddah contributors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-17"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/alturkestani/TrafficTwin"
keywords:
  - traffic simulation
  - digital twin
  - Eclipse SUMO
  - OpenStreetMap
  - Jeddah
  - transport policy
  - emergency response
abstract: >-
  A traffic digital twin of Jeddah built on Eclipse SUMO and OpenStreetMap: a city-wide
  mesoscopic model driven by a synthetic population for policy questions (remote work, staggered
  hours, day types, public transport, pricing, Loop tunnels), microscopic focus windows for events
  (crash, rain, flood, motorcade, evacuation), and an emergency strategist that ranks response
  plans for human approval. All results are synthetic demand, uncalibrated.
